{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-004-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs","line":4288,"method":"TrimBoringTail_SubOrbitalTerminal_RefusesTrim_ShapeMismatch","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingOptimizer.TailTrim.cs:169; make TailPreservesTerminalSpawnStateInternal return true for non-spawnable terminals -> trim proceeds and EndUT drops to about 140 -> red; recompiling the same fixture with a matching ecc of 0.01 leaves it green, so the named shape guard is never reached","what_it_asserts":"TrimBoringTail returns false and leaves EndUT=220 for a SubOrbital-terminal recording whose single tail OrbitSegment has ecc 0.05 vs terminal ecc 0.01.","why_weak":"TerminalState.SubOrbital is refused upfront by IsSpawnableTerminal (RecordingOptimizer.TailTrim.cs:169-175) and again by the switch default at :186-194, so OrbitShapeMatchesTerminal never runs and the 0.05 ecc row is inert. The sibling at line 4319 already pins the SubOrbital refusal with a refusal-log assertion, so this cell adds no distinct regression surface.","proposed_action":"Rename to name the terminal carve-out (or delete; 4319 keeps the observable), or use TerminalState.Orbiting with the mismatched shape so the shape path is actually exercised.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-004-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs","line":6256,"method":"OptimizationPass_PassiveDeorbitReentry_ProducesAscentExoReentryChain","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingOptimizer.cs:441; force IsGrazePattern to return true for every boundary -> no split, chainLength=1 -> red; a change that suppresses only ONE of the four boundaries (for example dropping SurfaceInvolved splits at RecordingOptimizer.cs:418) yields 4 segments and stays green under the >=4 bound","what_it_asserts":"RunOptimizationPass over a 5-section Surface/Atmo/Exo/Atmo/Surface recording yields at least 4 committed recordings.","why_weak":"The split pass loops until no candidates remain with maxSplitsPerPass=50 (RecordingStore.Optimization.cs:132), so the four boundaries produce exactly 5 segments. The >=4 tolerance was justified in the comment as a split-cap guard that cannot bind for this fixture, and it masks a regression that loses any single boundary.","proposed_action":"Assert the exact chain length (5) or assert the per-segment environment/phase sequence produced by the pass.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
